TI  - Antibiotic Exposure and Risk for Death or Bronchopulmonary Dysplasia in Very Low 
      Birth Weight Infants.
PG  - 289-293.e1
LID - S0022-3476(16)31230-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jpeds.2016.11.002 [doi]
AB  - We assessed the association between antibiotic exposure in the first 2 weeks of 
      life and development of bronchopulmonary dysplasia in a cohort of very low birth 
      weight infants. After controlling for the severity of illness, each additional 
      day of antibiotic therapy was associated with both an increased risk for and 
      severity of bronchopulmonary dysplasia.
