TI  - Early antibiotic exposure and the risk of necrotizing enterocolitis in preterm 
      neonates: insights from a large multicenter cohort in China.
PG  - 1196-1198
LID - 10.1038/s41390-025-04237-0 [doi]
AB  - The association between early antibiotic overuse in preterm neonates and the risk 
      of necrotizing enterocolitis (NEC) remains controversial. In this issue of 
      Pediatric Research, Zhu et al. present findings from a large multicenter 
      prospective cohort study across China, reporting no significant association 
      between early empirical antibiotic exposure and NEC. However, prolonged use of 
      broad-spectrum antibiotics was associated with increased mortality. The results 
      underscore the importance of antibiotic stewardship in neonatal care and 
      highlight the need for further randomized trials and mechanistic studies to 
      better understand the complex interactions between antibiotics and NEC 
      pathogenesis. IMPACT: This comment highlights the study by Zhu et al. 'Early 
      antibiotic exposure and necrotizing enterocolitis among preterm infants <34 
      weeks' gestation'.
