TI  - Empiric antibiotic prescribing practices for gram-positive coverage of late-onset 
      sepsis in neonatal intensive care units in North America.
PG  - 102-104
LID - 10.1017/ice.2024.176 [doi]
AB  - Late-onset sepsis (LOS) in the neonatal intensive care unit (NICU) causes 
      significant morbidity and mortality, yet guidance on empiric management is 
      limited. We surveyed NICUs across Canada and the United States regarding their 
      empiric antimicrobial regimens for LOS, thereby identifying large practice 
      variations and high rates of empiric vancomycin use.
