VI  - 20
IP  - 3
DP  - 2019 Mar
TI  - Antibiotic Resistance in the Neonatal Intensive Care Unit.
PG  - e135-e144
LID - 10.1542/neo.20-3-e135 [doi]
AB  - Antibiotic-resistant bacteria are an increasing problem in the NICU. Ineffective 
      empiric antibiotic therapy is associated with increased risk for morbidity and 
      mortality. Organisms that are resistant to multiple antimicrobial agents 
      (multidrug-resistant organisms) are particularly problematic. These organisms may 
      be transmitted to infants if infection control practices are not adhered to, or 
      they may be created by antibiotic exposure. Therefore, meticulous infection 
      prevention-including hand hygiene, surveillance cultures, contact precautions, 
      and selective decolonization-and antibiotic stewardship are important strategies 
      to minimize drug resistance in the NICU.
