TI  - A standardized guideline for antibiotic prophylaxis in surgical neonates().
PG  - 53-56
LID - S1055-8586(19)30009-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1053/j.sempedsurg.2019.01.009 [doi]
AB  - Infection following surgical procedures leads to increased morbidity and 
      mortality in all populations. Guidelines to aid providers in the proper use of 
      prophylactic antibiotics exist for adults, but are rare in the neonatal surgical 
      population. A recent emphasis on appropriate antibiotic stewardship had led to 
      the development of more guidelines without a coincident increase in surgical site 
      infection. Robust data from randomized, controlled trials, however, remain 
      sparse.
