TI  - [Initial antibiotic therapy in maternal-fetal infections which include ampicillin 
      even in countries where listeriosis is an incidental disease].
PG  - 117-8
AB  - Neonatal listeriosis is an exceptional disease in Northern Africa. Hence, 
      protocols for maternal-fetal infection treatment include only a third generation 
      cephalosporin and an aminoside. This protocol does not take into account the 
      possibility of Listeria monocytogenes infection. We report a fatal case of 
      neonatal listeriosis in Tunisia. The use of first antibiotics in maternal-foetal 
      infection must be reconsidered when lacking sufficient bacteriological data and 
      include systematically ampicillin in presumptive antibiotic protocols.
