DP  - 2005 Feb
TI  - Vertically acquired neonatal citrobacter brain abscess - case report and review 
      of the literature.
PG  - 188-90
AB  - Vertically acquired citrobacter meningitis in the neonate is very rare and 
      carries a very high mortality and morbidity. Overall, approximately 30% of 
      neonates with Citrobacter meningitis die and 50% sustain some damage to the CNS. 
      The authors describe a case of a newborn with Citrobacter koseri meningitis with 
      multiple brain abscesses, with a successful outcome following multiple burr-hole 
      aspirations and prolonged antibiotic therapy. An aggressive surgical approach 
      combined with intravenous antibiotics (including imipenems, to which the organism 
      is very sensitive) for a minimum of 4 weeks appears to improve the outcome of 
      infection with this virulent organism.
